<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sȳcŏphantor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sūc-</span></b> ),
		āri, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i> [id.], <i>to play the
				rogue</i>, <i>to deceive</i>, <i>trick</i>, <i>cheat</i> (Plautinian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ego nunc sucophantae huic sucophantari volo,</span>”
				<i>I have a mind to trick this trickster</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 4, 2, 116</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc me sucophantari pudet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 3, 58</span></i>
			.</div>
